{
  "_what": "Show rules: what decides whether anything Trillion would show (a notice, a tour, a layout, any later surface) shows, stays silent or is hidden, owned by src/workspace/show-rules.mjs. A rule is { id, label, subject, when, effect, until?, time_zone?, by?, made_at?, on? }: `subject` names what it is about (any key under `subjects`, which only gives the facts a person can pick from and their words; a surface passes its own thing whatever its subject), `when` is the formula engine's rule tree (parts/formula-engine/rules) over the subject's facts and the moment's facts below (null: always), `effect` is an `effects` row, and `until` ends it. An effect row marked `changes` (Changed) neither hides nor silences: its rule carries `set`, a list of { path, value } that change the thing's own fields where it holds, so one edit made on the canvas applies to exactly the things its `when` picks (this step, every step of a tour, every tour, a lasso of things) and is taken back by removing the rule. Moment facts: `clock` is now itself; `moment` names a value the caller knows about the moment (where it is shown, the device, whether the page was opened from a link) or one worked out from the time in the rule's own time zone (`hour`, `weekday`, named by `from_time`). `turns` says when that fact changes by itself (hour, day), so a page decides again then. `devices` say which device a page is on, by the first user_agent pattern it matches (an empty pattern matches any). `quick` are the choices offered on the thing itself: `until` as a span (`hours`) or the next time of day (`next_at_hour`), `device` limits the rule to the device it is set on; a quick rule is about things like this one, by the subject's `same_fact`, with the subject's `quick_effect`. `starting_rules` are rules everyone starts with; a person turns one off (or back on) in their own record. A subject marked `changed_only` is changed on the thing itself (Edit on canvas) and never offered for a bare rule in settings. A subject's `menu_heading` heads the menu on the thing; a choice fact's `values_from` says where the settings list reads the values a person can pick (a page `input` record, or a `route` and the `list` path in its answer, with each value's `id` and `label` paths, and a `parent` path when values nest: the controls are offered as the tree their dotted paths make, from every part's declarations). An effect row marked `shows` (Shown) is the strongest: where it holds the thing shows and is not silenced, so one thing a broader rule hides can be shown, for a while. Subject `control` is every control a part draws, named by the dotted path its part declares in its part.json `controls` (`sidebar.position`, `arrangement.header.tabs`, `open.open-beside`); `within` holds the path and every path it sits in, so a rule about `arrangement.header` holds for every control in a pane's header. `edit_rules` are the account's allow/deny rules for changing rules and types, evaluated by the shared rule-decision owner against the authenticated account owner or a named trusted reader, with optional conditions and expiry; absent `edit_rules`, `edit_authority.starting_rules` apply. Types are kept sets of rules (a preset, a kind of member): { id, label, inherits, rules }, a type taking every rule of the types it inherits at any depth. No type ships here: every type is a record a person keeps (`types` in their own show-rules record, switched on by `in_use`), and a giver gives one by sharing it. An account holds the types named in its cohorts (the giver's setup-context record), and a giver's rule carrying `audience` (a rule tree over the account facts, src/work-for-ais.json `facts`) is given to every account it holds for; given rules decide with the person's own and are listed as set for them. Adding a subject, a fact, an effect or a choice is a row here, and a type is a record a person keeps; nothing in code names one.",
  "record": "show-rules",
  "edit_authority": {
    "effects": [
      { "id": "allow", "label": "Allowed", "outcome": "allow", "strength": 1 },
      { "id": "deny", "label": "Not allowed", "outcome": "deny", "strength": 2 }
    ],
    "actions": ["change_rule", "remove_rule", "toggle_starting", "change_type", "remove_type", "change_edit_rules", "change_assignment", "change_attribute"],
    "facts": [
      { "id": "account_owner", "kind": "boolean" },
      { "id": "actor_kind", "kind": "choice" },
      { "id": "reader", "kind": "choice" },
      { "id": "action", "kind": "choice" },
      { "id": "now", "kind": "date" }
    ],
    "starting_rules": [
      { "id": "account-owner", "effect": "allow", "who": { "kind": "account_owner" }, "actions": ["change_rule", "remove_rule", "toggle_starting", "change_type", "remove_type", "change_edit_rules", "change_assignment", "change_attribute"] }
    ]
  },
